From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] psu: log unsupported scanned devices at debug level

The PSU scanner enumerates all hwmon and IIO devices. Filtering ADC, fan,
PECI and other non-PSU drivers is expected, not an error. Keep diagnostics
at debug level without changing device selection or genuine PSU errors.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
+++ b/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
@@ -410,10 +410,10 @@
                                      return a.second.name == pmbusName;
                                  }) == sensorTypes.end())
         {
-            // To avoid this error message, add your driver name to
-            // the pmbusNames vector at the top of this file.
-            lg2::error("'{NAME}' not found in sensor whitelist", "NAME",
-                       pmbusName);
+            // The scan includes non-PSU hwmon and IIO devices. Skipping
+            // drivers outside the supported PSU list is normal filtering.
+            lg2::debug("Skipping '{NAME}': not a supported PSU sensor driver",
+                       "NAME", pmbusName);
             continue;
         }
 
